          "number": 4,
          "letter": "D",
          "english": "The question regarding pay is also best avoided. To be frank, it's simply too early in the process for you to be the one who brings up salary expectations. \"Chances are if a candidate is participating in a phone interview, this is the first time they have talked with the company, and the first call isn't the appropriate time to talk about 'what's in it for you,'\" says Justina Strnad, the Talent Acquisition Manager for Shiftgig. \"Trust me, if you are a great candidate and make it to the next step, the hiring team is going to be very transparent about what's in it for you later on.\"",
          "chinese": "关于薪酬的问题也最好避免提出。坦率地说，现在还处于流程的早期阶段，不适合由你主动提出薪资预期。Shiftgig 人才招聘经理 Justina Strnad 说：“如果候选人正在参加电话面试，很可能这是他们第一次与公司交谈，而第一次通话并不适合讨论‘这对你有什么好处’。相信我，如果你是一名优秀的候选人，并且进入了下一阶段，招聘团队之后会非常透明地告诉你能得到什么。”",
