          "number": 6,
          "letter": "F",
          "english": "It seems basic, but surprisingly, a lot of people are late to phone interviews. \"About a quarter of the people with whom I schedule phone interviews aren't on time,\" says Sophie Cikovsky, who handles U.S. recruiting for Infinite Global. \"While this bothers me personally, it's also indicative of someone who isn't very detail-oriented,\" she explains. \"In order to identify this early in the hiring process, I started asking all candidates a few years ago to call me as opposed to calling them at an agreed-upon time. That way, if I hear from them at 1:13 p.m. or 12:49 p.m. instead of our planned 1:00 p.m. interview time, I have an early indicator that they might not be a great fit.\"",
          "chinese": "这似乎是基本要求，但令人意外的是，很多人参加电话面试时会迟到。负责 Infinite Global 美国招聘工作的 Sophie Cikovsky 说：“和我约定电话面试的人中，大约有四分之一无法准时参加。”她解释说：“虽然这件事让我个人感到恼火，但它也说明这个人可能不太注重细节。为了在招聘流程早期发现这一点，几年前我开始要求所有候选人在约定时间打电话给我，而不是由我打给他们。这样一来，如果我在下午1点13分或中午12点49分接到他们的电话，而不是在原定的下午1点面试时间接到，我就能及早判断他们可能并不十分适合这个职位。”",
