          "number": 9,
          "letter": "I",
          "english": "It's tough not to say things like \"um,\" \"uh,\" and \"like\" in everyday speech, but these verbal habits become much more pronounced when speaking on the phone, says Dardis. \"In face-to-face interviews, they're not as noticeable, because there are other things like your hair, suit, or body language to distract people.\" But in a phone interview, the only thing you have to go on is what you say and how you say it. \"That's why it's so important to eliminate these words from your speech when doing a phone interview.\"",
          "chinese": "Dardis 说，在日常谈话中，人们很难不说“嗯”“呃”和“就是”之类的话，但用电话交谈时，这些口头习惯会明显得多。“在面对面面试中，这些表达没有那么引人注意，因为还有头发、西装或肢体语言之类的其他因素会分散人们的注意力。”但在电话面试中，你能依靠的只有你说了什么以及你是如何表达的。“因此，进行电话面试时，从谈话中去掉这些词语非常重要。”",
